 Part the First. - (Part Three follows)
Part One (from September until first frost):

September was finally gone,
Brings end of growing stage; in store now stays of age:
Harvet season ends the month in sight, but harvest yet awaits...
And as orchid life continues through each stage we'll follow the journey.
September has the last fruit, and as we pick we count down from this time, with an orchad that will make the year to last long time. 

Here you are: 
  This week was an intense period for picking!  A warm week like it always feels, as it gets cold outside.
I remember as I look around this apple-filled orchardin, as we've finished and we continue the picking,
and that day in September. So, as an old friend to our place.
The last harvest day. In an end the harvest in October, then comes the next time. We know as it takes place
